desc: Calculated Risk (Casio VL-1 / KoniSynth port) by chmaha
tags: instrument synthesizer casio vl-1 vl-tone
author: chmaha
version: 1.2
changelog:
  Fix rhythms turning into continuous static in REAPER: the Tempo slider clashed with REAPER's built-in tempo variable.
about:
  Casio VL-1 (VL-Tone, 1979): monophonic pocket keyboard with a digital ADSR sound code, a rhythm box and a calculator.
  Sound engine ported from the Casio VL-1 engine of KoniSynth by k0n1m4k1, https://github.com/k0n1m4k1/KoniSynth (AGPL-3.0),
  which draws its waveforms, envelope, output stage and rhythm sounds from the PolyValens VL-1 emulator (2006, CC0/MIT),
  https://github.com/linuxmao-org/VL1-emulator.
  Casio and VL-Tone are trademarks of Casio Computer Co., Ltd.; no affiliation.
  JSFX version released under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0
  Claude generated some of this code
